// THE TSL PITFALL CASES (bench/skills/pitfall_harness.py; rules: bench/skills/pitfall_rules/tsl.py). Operator, 2026-09-30: "Yes to everything pending, queue it up lets go". Each quote is VERBATIM from the three.js r186 docs pinned at mrdoob/three.js@9b4a2ac (bench/skills/pitfalls/sources/three.js@9b4a2ac29c63: the manual's WebGPURenderer page and the TSL guide tsl/content/Guide.md, the successor of the wiki page "Three.js Shading Language"); MIT (the repository's LICENSE; no separate documentation licence). Prompts never name the good pattern (never_in_prompt). `examples` are the rules' own test (--self-test), written for this harness.
{"id": "tsl-detail-map-node-material", "area": "tsl", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "My three.js r186 app (TypeScript) renders through three's WebGPU build. This is the material module:\n\n```ts\nimport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\n\nconst loader = new THREE.TextureLoader();\nconst colorMap = loader.load('/textures/rock_color.jpg');\nconst detailMap = loader.load('/textures/rock_detail.jpg');\ndetailMap.wrapS = detailMap.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping;\n\nexport const groundMaterial = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ map: colorMap, roughness: 0.9 });\n```\n\nAdd a detail map to `groundMaterial`: sample `detailMap` with the UV coordinates scaled by 10 and multiply it into the base color, so close-up views show fine cracks. Give me the updated module in full.", "never_in_prompt": ["colorNode", "three/tsl", "NodeMaterial", "texture(", "uv(", "TSL"], "pitfall": ["tsl_glsl_material_hack"], "good": ["tsl_material_node_assigned", "tsl_imports_tsl"], "skills": [{"name": "threejs-llms-full-tsl-tsl-operators-14", "match": ["instead of raw GLSL", "Replace onBeforeCompile"]}, {"name": "threejs-llms-full-tsl-e-g", "match": ["Assign TSL nodes directly"]}], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/manual/#en/webgpurenderer", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/manual/pages/webgpurenderer.html", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/manual__pages__webgpurenderer.html", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "This part of your application must be ported to node materials and TSL."}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\n\nconst loader = new THREE.TextureLoader();\nconst colorMap = loader.load('/textures/rock_color.jpg');\nconst detailMap = loader.load('/textures/rock_detail.jpg');\ndetailMap.wrapS = detailMap.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping;\n\nexport const groundMaterial = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ map: colorMap, roughness: 0.9 });\ngroundMaterial.onBeforeCompile = (shader) => {\n  shader.uniforms.detailMap = { value: detailMap };\n  shader.fragmentShader = shader.fragmentShader\n    .replace('#define STANDARD', '#define STANDARD\\nuniform sampler2D detailMap;')\n    .replace('#include <map_fragment>', '#include <map_fragment>\\ndiffuseColor *= texture2D(detailMap, vMapUv * 10.0);');\n};", "good": "import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { texture, uv } from 'three/tsl';\n\nconst loader = new THREE.TextureLoader();\nconst colorMap = loader.load('/textures/rock_color.jpg');\nconst detailMap = loader.load('/textures/rock_detail.jpg');\ndetailMap.wrapS = detailMap.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping;\n\nconst detail = texture(detailMap, uv().mul(10));\n\nexport const groundMaterial = new THREE.MeshStandardNodeMaterial({ roughness: 0.9 });\ngroundMaterial.colorNode = texture(colorMap).mul(detail);"}}
{"id": "tsl-gpu-branch-not-js-if", "area": "tsl", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "three.js r186, TypeScript, WebGPU build. Write `src/terrain.ts` that exports `terrainColor`, a reusable shader function built with three's shading-language nodes from 'three/tsl': it takes a height (a float node) and returns a color node -- deep blue (0x1a3d8f) below 0.2, grass green (0x3c8d2f) below 0.6, snow white above that. Also export `terrainMaterial`, a `MeshStandardNodeMaterial` whose base color is `terrainColor` of each vertex's local y position.", "never_in_prompt": ["If(", "select(", "ElseIf", "Switch("], "pitfall": ["tsl_js_branch_on_node"], "good": ["tsl_gpu_branch"], "skills": [{"name": "r3f-tsl-hooks-18", "match": ["JavaScript if/else/for"]}, {"name": "web-gpu-compute-5", "match": ["TSL control flow is capitalized"]}], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/tsl/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/tsl/content/Guide.md", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/tsl__content__Guide.md", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "This differs from standard JavaScript `if` statements, which only run once on the CPU during the shader construction phase."}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import { MeshStandardNodeMaterial } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { Fn, color, positionLocal } from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport const terrainColor = Fn(([height]) => {\n  if (height.lessThan(0.2)) return color(0x1a3d8f);\n  if (height.lessThan(0.6)) return color(0x3c8d2f);\n  return color(0xffffff);\n});\n\nexport const terrainMaterial = new MeshStandardNodeMaterial();\nterrainMaterial.colorNode = terrainColor(positionLocal.y);", "good": "import { MeshStandardNodeMaterial } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { Fn, If, color, positionLocal } from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport const terrainColor = Fn(([height]) => {\n  const c = color(0xffffff).toVar();\n  If(height.lessThan(0.2), () => {\n    c.assign(color(0x1a3d8f));\n  }).ElseIf(height.lessThan(0.6), () => {\n    c.assign(color(0x3c8d2f));\n  });\n  return c;\n});\n\nexport const terrainMaterial = new MeshStandardNodeMaterial();\nterrainMaterial.colorNode = terrainColor(positionLocal.y);"}}
{"id": "tsl-uniform-value-not-rebuild", "area": "tsl", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "three.js r186, TypeScript, WebGPU build. My shield material:\n\n```ts\nimport { MeshStandardNodeMaterial } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { color, normalView, positionViewDirection } from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport const shieldMaterial = new MeshStandardNodeMaterial({ transparent: true });\nconst rim = normalView.dot(positionViewDirection).oneMinus().pow(3);\nshieldMaterial.colorNode = color(0x33aaff);\nshieldMaterial.emissiveNode = color(0x33aaff).mul(rim);\n```\n\nThe game UI has a color picker and a strength slider. Add `setShieldColor(hex: number)` and `setShieldStrength(s: number)` that the UI calls on every change -- many times a second while dragging -- so the shield's color and its rim glow strength follow them. Give me the module in full.", "never_in_prompt": ["uniform", ".value", "onFrameUpdate", "onRenderUpdate", "onObjectUpdate"], "pitfall": ["tsl_node_rebuilt_at_runtime"], "good": ["tsl_uniform_value_update"], "skills": [{"name": "threejs-llms-full-tsl-uniform-variables-18", "match": ["uniform(value"]}], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/tsl/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/tsl/content/Guide.md", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/tsl__content__Guide.md", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "Uniforms are useful to update values of variables like colors, lighting, or transformations without having to recreate the shader program."}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import { MeshStandardNodeMaterial } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { color, float, normalView, positionViewDirection } from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport const shieldMaterial = new MeshStandardNodeMaterial({ transparent: true });\nconst rim = normalView.dot(positionViewDirection).oneMinus().pow(3);\nlet tint = 0x33aaff;\nlet strength = 1;\nshieldMaterial.colorNode = color(tint);\nshieldMaterial.emissiveNode = color(tint).mul(rim);\n\nfunction rebuild() {\n  shieldMaterial.colorNode = color(tint);\n  shieldMaterial.emissiveNode = color(tint).mul(rim).mul(float(strength));\n  shieldMaterial.needsUpdate = true;\n}\n\nexport function setShieldColor(hex: number) {\n  tint = hex;\n  rebuild();\n}\n\nexport function setShieldStrength(s: number) {\n  strength = s;\n  rebuild();\n}", "good": "import { Color, MeshStandardNodeMaterial } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { normalView, positionViewDirection, uniform } from 'three/tsl';\n\nconst tint = uniform(new Color(0x33aaff));\nconst strength = uniform(1);\n\nexport const shieldMaterial = new MeshStandardNodeMaterial({ transparent: true });\nconst rim = normalView.dot(positionViewDirection).oneMinus().pow(3);\nshieldMaterial.colorNode = tint;\nshieldMaterial.emissiveNode = tint.mul(rim).mul(strength);\n\nexport function setShieldColor(hex: number) {\n  tint.value.setHex(hex);\n}\n\nexport function setShieldStrength(s: number) {\n  strength.value = s;\n}"}}
{"id": "tsl-compute-particles", "area": "tsl", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "three.js r186, TypeScript, WebGPU build (`import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu'`, the renderer is a `THREE.WebGPURenderer`). Write `src/snow.ts` exporting `createSnow(renderer: THREE.WebGPURenderer, count: number): { object: THREE.Object3D; update(dt: number): void }` for a snowfall of count = 1,000,000 flakes in a 20 x 20 x 20 box centred on the origin. Each flake falls at its own random speed (0.5 to 2 units per second) and wraps from y = -10 back to y = 10; `update(dt)` is called once per frame from the render loop. It must hold 60 fps with a million flakes.", "never_in_prompt": [".compute(", "compute(", "instancedArray", "instanceIndex", "Fn(", "storage", "computeAsync", "three/tsl"], "pitfall": ["tsl_cpu_buffer_loop"], "good": ["tsl_compute_dispatched"], "skills": ["tsl-compute-shaders", {"name": "web-gpu-compute-5", "match": ["renderer.compute(computeNodes"]}], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/tsl/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/tsl/content/Guide.md", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/tsl__content__Guide.md", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "The **Compute Stage** allows you to perform general-purpose parallel computations (GPGPU) directly on the GPU using compute shaders.", "gap": "no armed library skill teaches the TSL compute pattern (a Fn(...)().compute(count) node over instancedArray storage, dispatched with renderer.compute); threejs-llms-full-tsl-compute-shader-lifecycle-2 is quarantined; `tsl-compute-shaders` is to be built from the guide through the ONE pipeline"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\n\nexport function createSnow(renderer: THREE.WebGPURenderer, count: number) {\n  const positions = new Float32Array(count * 3);\n  const speeds = new Float32Array(count);\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n    positions[i * 3] = Math.random() * 20 - 10;\n    positions[i * 3 + 1] = Math.random() * 20 - 10;\n    positions[i * 3 + 2] = Math.random() * 20 - 10;\n    speeds[i] = 0.5 + Math.random() * 1.5;\n  }\n  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(positions, 3));\n  const object = new THREE.Points(geometry, new THREE.PointsMaterial({ size: 0.03 }));\n  function update(dt: number) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n      let y = positions[i * 3 + 1] - speeds[i] * dt;\n      if (y < -10) y += 20;\n      positions[i * 3 + 1] = y;\n    }\n    geometry.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;\n  }\n  return { object, update };\n}", "good": "import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { Fn, If, hash, instanceIndex, instancedArray, uniform, vec3 } from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport function createSnow(renderer: THREE.WebGPURenderer, count: number) {\n  const positions = instancedArray(count, 'vec3');\n  const speeds = instancedArray(count, 'float');\n  const delta = uniform(0);\n\n  const init = Fn(() => {\n    positions.element(instanceIndex).assign(vec3(\n      hash(instanceIndex).mul(20).sub(10),\n      hash(instanceIndex.add(1)).mul(20).sub(10),\n      hash(instanceIndex.add(2)).mul(20).sub(10)));\n    speeds.element(instanceIndex).assign(hash(instanceIndex.add(3)).mul(1.5).add(0.5));\n  })().compute(count);\n\n  const step = Fn(() => {\n    const p = positions.element(instanceIndex);\n    p.y.subAssign(speeds.element(instanceIndex).mul(delta));\n    If(p.y.lessThan(-10), () => {\n      p.y.addAssign(20);\n    });\n  })().compute(count);\n\n  renderer.compute(init);\n\n  const material = new THREE.SpriteNodeMaterial();\n  material.positionNode = positions.toAttribute();\n  material.scaleNode = uniform(0.03);\n  const object = new THREE.Sprite(material);\n  object.count = count;\n  object.frustumCulled = false;\n\n  function update(dt: number) {\n    delta.value = dt;\n    renderer.compute(step);\n  }\n  return { object, update };\n}"}}
{"id": "tsl-imports-webgpu-and-tsl-entries", "area": "tsl", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "three.js r186, TypeScript, Vite. Write `src/materials/hologram.ts` exporting `createHologramMaterial()`: an unlit, transparent, additive node material for a sci-fi hologram, built from three's shading-language node functions -- a cyan rim glow from the view angle (Fresnel-style, from the view-space normal and the view direction), horizontal scanlines that scroll upward over time, and a slight flicker. Include the imports.", "never_in_prompt": ["three/tsl", "three/webgpu"], "pitfall": ["tsl_legacy_node_import"], "good": ["tsl_webgpu_entry_imports"], "skills": [{"name": "web-gpu-allocation-gc-1", "match": ["import THREE from 'three/webgpu'"]}], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/manual/#en/webgpurenderer", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/manual/pages/webgpurenderer.html", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/manual__pages__webgpurenderer.html", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "`WebGPURenderer` has different build files so the way you import three.js changes:"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import { AdditiveBlending } from 'three';\nimport { MeshBasicNodeMaterial, color, normalView, positionViewDirection, positionWorld, time, float, hash } from 'three/examples/jsm/nodes/Nodes.js';\n\nexport function createHologramMaterial() {\n  const material = new MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ transparent: true, blending: AdditiveBlending, depthWrite: false });\n  const rim = normalView.dot(positionViewDirection).oneMinus().pow(2);\n  const lines = positionWorld.y.mul(40).sub(time.mul(4)).fract().step(0.5);\n  const flicker = hash(time.floor()).mul(0.2).add(0.8);\n  material.colorNode = color(0x33ffff);\n  material.opacityNode = rim.add(lines.mul(0.3)).mul(flicker);\n  return material;\n}", "good": "import { AdditiveBlending, MeshBasicNodeMaterial } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { color, hash, normalView, positionViewDirection, positionWorld, time } from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport function createHologramMaterial() {\n  const material = new MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ transparent: true, blending: AdditiveBlending, depthWrite: false });\n  const rim = normalView.dot(positionViewDirection).oneMinus().pow(2);\n  const lines = positionWorld.y.mul(40).sub(time.mul(4)).fract().step(0.5);\n  const flicker = hash(time.floor()).mul(0.2).add(0.8);\n  material.colorNode = color(0x33ffff);\n  material.opacityNode = rim.add(lines.mul(0.3)).mul(flicker);\n  return material;\n}"}}
{"id": "tsl-setup-new-vite-project", "area": "tsl", "kind": "setup", "prompt": "Start a new three.js project (three r186, Vite, TypeScript) whose materials will be written in TSL, three.js's node-based shading language. Give me package.json, index.html and src/main.ts: a full-window canvas with a spinning cube whose color pulses over time, lit by a directional light, resizing with the window.", "never_in_prompt": ["three/webgpu", "three/tsl", "WebGPURenderer", "setAnimationLoop", "renderer.init", "NodeMaterial"], "pitfall": ["tsl_webgl_renderer", "tsl_legacy_node_import", "tsl_webgpu_render_before_init"], "good": ["tsl_webgpu_entry_imports", "tsl_webgpu_renderer_ready"], "skills": [{"name": "web-gpu-allocation-gc-1", "match": ["import THREE from 'three/webgpu'"]}, "tsl-webgpu-setup"], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/manual/#en/webgpurenderer", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/manual/pages/webgpurenderer.html", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/manual__pages__webgpurenderer.html", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "It's important to understand that WebGPU is initialized in an asynchronous fashion.", "gap": "no armed library skill carries the manual's WebGPU renderer setup (setAnimationLoop, or await init() before an own loop; web-gpu-allocation-gc-1 carries only the import entries); `tsl-webgpu-setup` is to be built from it through the ONE pipeline"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "package.json\n```json\n{\"name\": \"tsl-app\", \"private\": true, \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": {\"dev\": \"vite\", \"build\": \"tsc && vite build\"}, \"dependencies\": {\"three\": \"^0.186.0\"}, \"devDependencies\": {\"@types/three\": \"^0.186.0\", \"typescript\": \"^5.9.0\", \"vite\": \"^7.0.0\"}}\n```\nindex.html\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /><title>TSL app</title>\n    <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;overflow:hidden}</style></head>\n  <body>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.ts\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\nsrc/main.ts\n```ts\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { MeshStandardNodeMaterial, color, sin, time } from 'three/nodes';\n\nconst renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\nrenderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\ndocument.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\nconst scene = new THREE.Scene();\nconst camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(60, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 100);\ncamera.position.z = 3;\nscene.add(new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 2));\nconst material = new MeshStandardNodeMaterial();\nmaterial.colorNode = color(0x3399ff).mul(sin(time).mul(0.5).add(0.5));\nconst cube = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(), material);\nscene.add(cube);\naddEventListener('resize', () => {\n  camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n  renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n});\nfunction loop() {\n  requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n  cube.rotation.y += 0.01;\n  renderer.render(scene, camera);\n}\nloop();\n```", "good": "package.json\n```json\n{\"name\": \"tsl-app\", \"private\": true, \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": {\"dev\": \"vite\", \"build\": \"tsc && vite build\"}, \"dependencies\": {\"three\": \"^0.186.0\"}, \"devDependencies\": {\"@types/three\": \"^0.186.0\", \"typescript\": \"^5.9.0\", \"vite\": \"^7.0.0\"}}\n```\nindex.html\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /><title>TSL app</title>\n    <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;overflow:hidden}</style></head>\n  <body>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.ts\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\nsrc/main.ts\n```ts\nimport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { color, sin, time } from 'three/tsl';\n\nconst renderer = new THREE.WebGPURenderer({ antialias: true });\nrenderer.setPixelRatio(devicePixelRatio);\nrenderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\nrenderer.setAnimationLoop(render);\ndocument.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\nconst scene = new THREE.Scene();\nconst camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(60, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 100);\ncamera.position.z = 3;\nscene.add(new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 2));\nconst material = new THREE.MeshStandardNodeMaterial();\nmaterial.colorNode = color(0x3399ff).mul(sin(time).mul(0.5).add(0.5));\nconst cube = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(), material);\nscene.add(cube);\naddEventListener('resize', () => {\n  camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n  camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n  renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n});\nfunction render() {\n  cube.rotation.y += 0.01;\n  renderer.render(scene, camera);\n}\n```"}}
{"id": "tsl-setup-importmap-page", "area": "tsl", "kind": "setup", "example_lang": "html", "prompt": "Make a single index.html -- no bundler, no build step -- that loads three.js r186 from the jsDelivr CDN as ES modules and shows a rotating torus knot whose material is written in TSL (three.js's shading language): its color shifts with the surface normal and over time. Everything in that one file.", "never_in_prompt": ["three/webgpu", "three/tsl", "three.webgpu.js", "three.tsl.js", "WebGPURenderer", "setAnimationLoop"], "pitfall": ["tsl_importmap_missing_webgpu_build", "tsl_webgl_renderer", "tsl_legacy_node_import", "tsl_webgpu_render_before_init"], "good": ["tsl_importmap_webgpu_build", "tsl_webgpu_entry_imports", "tsl_webgpu_renderer_ready"], "skills": [{"name": "web-gpu-allocation-gc-1", "match": ["import THREE from 'three/webgpu'"]}, "tsl-webgpu-setup"], "packages": ["three"], "source": {"url": "https://threejs.org/manual/#en/webgpurenderer", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrdoob/three.js/9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8/manual/pages/webgpurenderer.html", "commit": "9b4a2ac29c63ccb43fd51c5661f2f873ac2c39b8", "file": "three.js@9b4a2ac29c63/manual__pages__webgpurenderer.html", "licence": "MIT (three.js LICENSE at 9b4a2ac, r186; the repository carries no separate documentation licence)", "quote": "If you are using an import map, it's recommended to change it to the following (the paths differ depending on your setup):", "gap": "no armed library skill carries the manual's import map for the WebGPU build (three.webgpu.js, three.tsl.js) or its renderer initialization (web-gpu-allocation-gc-1 carries only the import entries); `tsl-webgpu-setup` is to be built from it through the ONE pipeline"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<body style=\"margin:0\">\n<script type=\"importmap\">\n{ \"imports\": {\n  \"three\": \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.186.0/build/three.module.js\",\n  \"three/addons/\": \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/